          "case_name": "In re Interest of DeWayne G., Jr.",
          "citation": "263 Neb. 43, 638 N.W.2d 510 (2002)",
          "court": "Nebraska Supreme Court",
          "year": 2002,
          "date_decided": "2002-01-25",
          "holding": "The court held that Neb. Rev. Stat. § 43-283.01 gives a parent no right to demand a separate pre-termination hearing on whether reasonable efforts to preserve and reunify the family were made, and reinstated the termination of parental rights.",
          "relevance": "The court notes that priority must be given to preserving and reunifying the family even when adoption or guardianship efforts proceed concurrently.",
          "quote": "the plain language of § 43-283.01 contains no such directive granting a parent or any other party the right to bring a motion requesting a \"separate hearing\"",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/1810106/in-re-dewayne-g-jr/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 1810106
        },
        {
          "case_name": "In re Interest of Leyton C. & Landyn C.",
          "citation": "307 Neb. 529, 949 N.W.2d 773 (2020)",
          "court": "Nebraska Supreme Court",
          "year": 2020,
          "date_decided": "2020-10-23",
          "holding": "The court held that the State proved by clear and convincing evidence both a statutory ground under § 43-292 and that termination was in the children's best interests, and reversed the Court of Appeals' contrary decision.",
          "relevance": "The mother's failure over the case's life to correct the conditions that caused removal is what foreclosed reunification.",
          "quote": "The State proved by clear and convincing evidence that Madison neglected to provide necessary parental care and protection for her children.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4848107/in-re-interest-of-leyton-c-landyn-c/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 4848107
        },
        {
          "case_name": "In re Interest of Rylee S.",
