          "court": "Nebraska Supreme Court",
          "year": 2013,
          "date_decided": "2013-04-25",
          "holding": "The court held that a dispositional order compelling the mother to release her mental health records and submit to a pretreatment assessment was unreasonable because the juvenile court made no supporting findings of fact and the order did not tend to correct or ameliorate the conditions on which the adjudication was based.",
          "relevance": "A plan untethered to the adjudicated conditions cannot advance reunification and will not be sustained on appeal.",
          "quote": "we find that the dispositional plan and subsequent order in this case were unreasonable",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/906379/in-re-interest-of-rylee-s/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 906379
        }
